`extractReachableGraph(graph, start)` receives a finite directed graph represented as an object whose values are arrays of outgoing neighbor names. A referenced node absent from `graph` is a leaf. Traverse from `start` and return an object containing every reachable node as a key and that node's outgoing-neighbor array as its value.

The returned graph must be structurally independent of the input: every returned neighbor array must be a fresh array. Mutating a returned array must not change `graph`, and mutating an input neighbor array after the call must not change the returned graph. Do not mutate the input during extraction.

Use only standard JavaScript. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, packages, or frameworks. Return a corrected complete source file.

```javascript
function extractReachableGraph(graph, start) {
  const result = {};
  const visited = new Set();

  function visit(node) {
    if (visited.has(node)) {
      return;
    }

    visited.add(node);
    const neighbors = graph[node] || [];
    result[node] = neighbors;

    for (const neighbor of neighbors) {
      visit(neighbor);
    }
  }

  visit(start);
  return result;
}

module.exports = extractReachableGraph;
