Each record is `(id, baseline, current)`, and every baseline is strictly positive. Return the IDs ordered by decreasing relative change, where a record's relative change is `(current - baseline) / baseline`.

Compare these ratios exactly using integer arithmetic; do not convert them to floating-point values. The full `i64` range is permitted for `current`, so intermediate subtraction and cross-multiplication must not overflow. Records with mathematically equal relative changes must retain their original input order. Duplicate IDs are allowed and remain separate records.

Use only the standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, or external packages.","reference_code":"pub fn order_by_relative_change(records: &[(u32, i64, i64)]) -> Vec<u32> {
    let mut positions: Vec<usize> = (0..records.len()).collect();

    positions.sort_by(|&left_index, &right_index| {
        let (_, left_baseline, left_current) = records[left_index];
        let (_, right_baseline, right_current) = records[right_index];

        let left_delta = left_current as i128 - left_baseline as i128;
        let right_delta = right_current as i128 - right_baseline as i128;
        let left_scaled = left_delta * right_baseline as i128;
        let right_scaled = right_delta * left_baseline as i128;

        right_scaled.cmp(&left_scaled)
    });

    positions
        .into_iter()
        .map(|index| records[index].0)
        .collect()
}
","known_bad_code":"pub fn order_by_relative_change(records: &[(u32, i64, i64)]) -> Vec<u32> {
    let mut positions: Vec<usize> = (0..records.len()).collect();

    positions.sort_unstable_by(|&left_index, &right_index| {
        let (_, left_baseline, left_current) = records[left_index];
        let (_, right_baseline, right_current) = records[right_index];

        let left_delta = left_current as i128 - left_baseline as i128;
        let right_delta = right_current as i128 - right_baseline as i128;
        let left_scaled = left_delta * right_baseline as i128;
        let right_scaled = right_delta * left_baseline as i128;

        right_scaled.cmp(&left_scaled)
    });

    positions
        .into_iter()
        .map(|index| records[index].0)
        .collect()
}
","known_bad_label":"The implementation uses an unstable sort, so records with mathematically equal relative changes are not guaranteed to retain their original input order."}]}

